--- a/.andromeda/test-plan.md
+++ b/.andromeda/test-plan.md
@@ -24,3 +24,2 @@
 decision/failed-load-ends-settle-wait · Failed load ends the settle wait — A failed load ends the harness and driver settle wait, so a failed stylesheet does not leave the document not settled on loads for good. · why: the harness test a_failed_stylesheet_reaches_the_document_through_the_counter_and_unblocks_it pins it, and the driver's load wait settles through the same harness settle
-decision/key-after-dropped-anonymous-block · Key press after a dropped anonymous block — A key press on a focused control whose anonymous block was dropped does not panic, focus stays and the key still acts. · why: key_press_after_container_lost_its_box pins no panic, focus staying and the key still moving a select's choice, in both layout modes
 decision/mcp-causes-served-with-remedy · Refusal causes served with their remedy over MCP — Every refusal cause a tool call reaches is served through MCP with its remedy. · why: ratified · guard: stand_mcp_tools · except: unknown-verb is not served through MCP
@@ -101,3 +100,3 @@
 decision/contrast-reader-reads-only · Contrast reader changes nothing — The harness's contrast readers, of an element's text and of an open list's highlighted row, read and change nothing: no mutation, input, pump or settle.
-decision/count-and-rename-sweeps · Verb-count and test-rename sweeps — A change of the driver's verb count sweeps the tests and examples for pins of the verb table's length and of its indices, and a test rename sweeps the old name held as a string literal, such as a requirement's witness. · why: A word sweep misses a numeric pin and a test name held as a string. · except: A test name holding a count word that another check pins as a witness string is kept by a count sweep, the name searched before any rename.
+decision/count-and-rename-sweeps · Verb-count and test-rename sweeps — A change of the driver's verb count or of a CI leg's file count sweeps the tests, examples and CI-script tests for pins of that count held as a literal, and a test rename sweeps the old name held as a string literal, such as a requirement's witness. · why: A word sweep misses a numeric pin and a test name held as a string. · except: A test name holding a count word that another check pins as a witness string is kept by a count sweep, the name searched before any rename.
 decision/cross-os-readings-by-answer-digest · Cross-OS readings of the served tasks — The seven served tasks are read on every CI OS by one stand check that compares the driver's answer digests for snapshot (every part), lint and actions, at boot and after one acting step in both layout modes, to one committed table, with no shot and no kept check file. · guard: stand_cross_os_readings
@@ -322,2 +321,3 @@
 decision/fast-jobs-gate-the-rest · Fast jobs gate the rest — The four fast CI jobs need nothing and every other job needs all four. · guard: CiWorkflowTest
+decision/focus-test-pins-where-focus-lands · Focus tests pin where focus lands — A focus test pins the node focus lands on, never only that a hidden control is not focused. · why: Once the post-layout focus fixup runs, an assertion that a hidden control is not focused holds with or without the change under test.
 decision/harness-graph-tests-enable-accessibility · Harness graph unit tests turn accessibility on — A harness unit test of the UI graph turns the accessibility feature on through its dev-dependency, for the test build only. · why: A per-package test build leaves the accessibility feature off, and the UI graph is gated by it.
@@ -453,2 +453,3 @@
 decision/no-screenshot-in-recorded-check-scripts · No screenshot step in committed recorded checks — The scripts that record the committed checks hold no `screenshot` step, so the kept checks stay byte-equal across operating systems. · why: a shot's PNG bytes differ by OS · guard: the_committed_checks_are_what_the_binary_records
+decision/render-wait-by-stored-waker · Render waits leave the waker to the producer — A test task that waits for a later render on the Dioxus bridge leaves its waker for the producer to wake and never wakes its own waker while it waits. · why: A task that wakes its own waker while it waits livelocks inside the buffered render, a limit asserted by no check.
 decision/select-list-painted-by-paint-scene · Select list painted by the scene painter alone — The harness, the session and the binary drive the select list headlessly because the list paints through `paint_scene` alone, with no shell or renderer code of its own. · why: the harness screenshot, the session's screenshot of an open-list row in stand_act_popup and select_popup_painted all read the open list with no shell present
